  "report_period": "Week 43 (17th Oct to 24th Oct 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "2020 Bulkers have committed their Newcastlemax \"Bulk Sao Paulo\" 208/2020 New Times, China (SS 06/2030, DD 06/2028, Scrubber fitted) to clients of Ebe NV at USD 72,75 mill. Remind you that a month ago, same owners sold the three sister vessels \"Bulk Sandefjord\" 208/2019 New Times, China (SS 08/2029, DD 03/2027, Scrubber fitted, \"Bulk Santiago\" 208/2019 New Times, China (SS 09/2029, DD 03/2027, Scrubber fitted) & \"Bulk Shenzen\" 208/2020 New Times, China (SS 01/2030, DD 01/2028, Scrubber fitted) at USD 209 mill enbloc. The Capesize \"Mineral Subic\" 179/2011 Hanjin, Korea (SS/DD 05/2026) was committed to Chinese interests at USD 30,25 mill. Note that a couple of months ago, the one-year-older \"Frontier Bonanza\" 179/2010 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 10/2025) was sold at USD 26,2 mill. Moreover, the \"AP Power\" 173/2006 Bohai, China (SS/DD 09/2026) was committed at USD 14,5 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Cape Veni\" 173/2007 Bohai, China (SS 07/2027, DD 07/2025) was sold back in June at USD 17 mill. On the Supramax sector, Ever Prosperity Shipping committed the \"Sea Dana\" 57/2009 Jiangsu, China (SS 05/2029, DD 10/2026) at USD 11 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Marinor\" 56/2009 Jiangsu, China (SS 07/2029, DD 05/2028) was sold a month ago at USD 10,8 mill. Furthermore, the \"Xie Hai Yong Feng\" 52/2001 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 06/2026, DD 07/2026) was committed at USD 6,8 mill, while the one-year-younger \"JW Flora\" 53/2002 Oshima, Japan (SS 07/2027, DD 10/2025) was sold a week ago at USD 6,8 mill also. The Handysize \"Danship Bulker\" 28/2009 I-S, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 02/2027) was committed to Vietnamese interests at mid-high USD 8 mill. Note that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Bright Hope\" 28/2010 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 9,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Following the sale of the VLCC \"Monaco Loyalty\" 307/2007 Dalian, China (SS 07/2027, DD 10/2025) in September at USD 42 mill, clients of Sinokor have now committed the sister vessel \"Singapore Loyalty\" 307/2007 Dalian, China (SS 10/2027, DD 11/2025) at USD 46,5 mill. Chemikalien Seetransport have committed the LR1 \"Chemtrans Cancale\" 73/2007 New Century, China (SS 06/2027, DD 03/2026) to undisclosed interests at USD 12 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the sister vessel \"Fair Winds\" 74/2007 New Century, China (SS 09/2027, DD 11/2025) was sold at USD 11 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid/high usd 10,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 16,000/18,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 17,000/20,000 pd range. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Indian trips via South Africa into India were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US Gulf or North Coast South America were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. Continental trips via North Coast South America into West Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 17,000/20,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 27,000/28,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 18,250 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 550K. East Coast South American trips into South Africa were reported at the level of usd 28,000/29,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/700K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Trips from China into India were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 16,000/17,000 pd range. Indian trips via Indonesia into India were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/15,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China into India were fixed around usd 18,000/19,000 pd. West African trips into Continent-Mediterranean range were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. West African trips into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 16,000/17,000 pd. Continental trips into West African were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Continental trips into South America were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Continental trips into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 17,000/18,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into Baltic were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. South American coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 21,000/23,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
